It gives us a sense of reassurance. And this is why liberals like to watch the pundits on MSNBC and conservatives like to watch the pundits on Fox. A more cautious style that sort of says, the chance that Donald Trump is going to be impeached is 11.3% or the chance that you're going to die from cancer is 65.3%. These estimates run up against a very powerful psychological impulse we have for certainty that we actually want someone to hold our hand and tell us you're not going to die. We don't want a probability estimate.
我们实际上希望得到事情会如我们所愿发展的保证。所以这是我对你的最后一个问题。如果有人建议人们做一些违背他们对幸福和安心的情感需求的事情，我预测这个建议，无论出于多么良好的意愿，无论多么准确，很可能不会被大多数人采纳。你对我的预测有什么看法，菲尔？嗯，我认为你所说的话中有很多真实之处。我认为人们在思考未来时，有很多目标，他们希望确认自己对意识形态阵营的忠诚。

